# Cross-harness continuation

When resuming existing repository work, use `cross-harness-handoff` to check shared ECC project memory before asking the user to repeat context. Verify recalled state against current Git/source/spec/ADR; the repository is authoritative. Pass its absolute Git root as `workspaceRoot` to ECC MCP calls. For a harness/session transfer, save a concise durable handoff through that skill. Details stay on-demand at `~/.agents/skills/cross-harness-handoff/SKILL.md`.

# Browser verification

For relevant interactive browser/frontend QA, prefer a functional native browser tool; otherwise load `agent-browser` on demand. Antigravity uses its native Browser Subagent/Chrome DevTools. Use uniquely named isolated sessions and close your own session afterward. Scope browser checks to actual browser implications; no automatic browser launch for backend-only, browser-unrelated C++/C#, documentation-only, unrelated Git, or trivial non-browser work. Choose one frontend owner: `impeccable` normally, `redesign-existing-projects` for requested whole-app redesign; differentiated image/style requests use their specialist. User/project brand and supplied references win.
